IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`

-- ccc26-probation.l4 -- sections 731, 731.1, 732 and 732.1(2) to (7) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the making of a probation order,
-- the firearms prohibitions, the intermittent sentence, and the conditions of a probation order and the court's obligations (lines 15497-15571 of the text).
-- Layer 1 of part ccc26. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. Terms of imprisonment are compared with the helper of ccc26-interpretation.

§ `Section 731 -- Making of probation order`

-- (1)(a): a grant "if no minimum punishment is prescribed by law" (an "if" gate on a grant: NOTHING when it fails).
-- src:15497 | Probation
-- src:15498 | Making of probation order
-- src:15499 | 731 (1) Where a person is convicted of an offence, a court may, having regard to the age and character of the offender, the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission,
-- src:15500 | (a) if no minimum punishment is prescribed by law, suspend the passing of sentence and direct that the offender be released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order; or
@ref s 731(1)(a) (src:15497-15500)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a minimum punishment is prescribed by law for the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 731(1)(a) the court may suspend the passing of sentence and direct that the offender be released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order` MEANS   -- gate: where (a person is convicted of an offence), if (no minimum punishment is prescribed by law)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is convicted of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence, a court may"
        IF `a minimum punishment is prescribed by law for the offence` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence has a minimum punishment is for the offence section
        IF `a minimum punishment is prescribed by law for the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if no minimum punishment is prescribed by law, suspend the passing of sentence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1)(b): a probation order "in addition to fining or sentencing the offender to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years". The cap limits the grant in the
-- text's own wording and is not inside the "Where" clause, so a term over two years answers NOTHING (fork row; the other reading is JUST FALSE).
-- src:15497 | Probation
-- src:15498 | Making of probation order
-- src:15499 | 731 (1) Where a person is convicted of an offence, a court may, having regard to the age and character of the offender, the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission,
@ref s 731(1)(b) (src:15497-15499)
-- src:15501 | (b) in addition to fining or sentencing the offender to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, direct that the offender comply with the conditions prescribed in a probation order.
@ref s 731(1)(b) (src:15501)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court fines the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the imprisonment the court imposes` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 731(1)(b) the court may direct that the offender comply with the conditions prescribed in a probation order in addition to the fine or imprisonment` MEANS   -- gate: where (a person is convicted of an offence); limit of the grant (imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is convicted of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence, a court may"
        IF `the imprisonment the court imposes` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated` AND `the court fines the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the imprisonment the court imposes` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in addition to fining or sentencing the offender to imprisonment"
        IF `s 731(1)(b) the term of imprisonment is at most two years` `the imprisonment the court imposes` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years"

-- helper of (1)(b): the term imposed is at most two years (a plain comparison, not a grant).
@ref s 731(1)(b) (src:15501)
GIVEN `the imprisonment the court imposes` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 731(1)(b) the term of imprisonment is at most two years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the imprisonment the court imposes`
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- HELPER
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST FALSE   -- HELPER
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN `s 716 the first period is at most the second period` term `two years`

-- src:15502 | Idem
-- src:15503 | (2) A court may also make a probation order where it discharges an accused under subsection 730(1).
@ref s 731(2) (src:15502-15503)
GIVEN `the court discharges the accused under subsection 730(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 731(2) the court may make a probation order` MEANS   -- gate: where (it discharges an accused under subsection 730(1))
    IF `the court discharges the accused under subsection 730(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court may also make a probation order where it discharges an accused under subsection 730(1)"

-- src:15504 | (3.1) [Repealed, 1997, c. 17, s. 1]
@ref s 731(3.1) (src:15504)
`s 731(3.1), repealed` MEANS "[Repealed, 1997, c. 17, s. 1]"

§ `Section 731.1 -- Firearms, etc., prohibitions`

-- src:15505 | Firearm, etc., prohibitions
-- src:15506 | 731.1 (1) Before making a probation order, the court shall consider whether section 109 or 110 is applicable.
@ref s 731.1(1) (src:15505-15506)
GIVEN `the court is about to make a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 731.1(1) the court must consider whether section 109 or 110 is applicable` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to make a probation order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before making a probation order, the court shall consider whether section 109 or 110 is applicable"

-- src:15507 | Application of section 109 or 110
-- src:15508 | (2) For greater certainty, a condition of a probation order referred to in paragraph 732.1(3)(d) does not affect the operation of section 109 or 110.
@ref s 731.1(2) (src:15507-15508)
GIVEN `the condition is one referred to in paragraph 732.1(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 731.1(2) the condition leaves the operation of section 109 or 110 unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the condition is one referred to in paragraph 732.1(3)(d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a condition of a probation order referred to in paragraph 732.1(3)(d) does not affect the operation of section 109 or 110"

§ `Section 732 -- Intermittent sentence`

-- (1): the sentence of imprisonment of "ninety days or less", whether in default of payment of a fine or otherwise.
-- src:15509 | Intermittent sentence
-- src:15510 | 732 (1) Where the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of ninety days or less on an offender convicted of an offence, whether in default of payment of a fine or otherwise, the court may, having regard to the age and character of the offender, the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission, and the availability of appropriate accommodation to ensure compliance with the sentence, order
-- src:15511 | (a) that the sentence be served intermittently at such times as are specified in the order; and
-- src:15512 | (b) that the offender comply with the conditions prescribed in a probation order when not in confinement during the period that the sentence is being served and, if the court so orders, on release from prison after completing the intermittent sentence.
@ref s 732(1) (src:15509-15512)
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on an offender convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment imposed` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732(1)(a) the court may order that the sentence be served intermittently at such times as are specified in the order` MEANS   -- gate: where (the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of ninety days or less on an offender convicted of an offence)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on an offender convicted of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of ninety days or less on an offender convicted of an offence"
        IF `s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `the term of imprisonment imposed` `ninety days` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a sentence of imprisonment of ninety days or less"
        IF `s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `the term of imprisonment imposed` `ninety days` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the term is ninety days or less is not settled by the calendar
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732(1)(b) (src:15509-15512)
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on an offender convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment imposed` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732(1)(b) the court may order that the offender comply with the conditions prescribed in a probation order when not in confinement` MEANS   -- gate: where (a sentence of ninety days or less on an offender convicted of an offence)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on an offender convicted of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of ninety days or less on an offender convicted of an offence"
        IF `s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `the term of imprisonment imposed` `ninety days` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a sentence of imprisonment of ninety days or less"
        IF `s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `the term of imprisonment imposed` `ninety days` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the term is ninety days or less is not settled by the calendar
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15513 | Application to vary intermittent sentence
-- src:15514 | (2) An offender who is ordered to serve a sentence of imprisonment intermittently may, on giving notice to the prosecutor, apply to the court that imposed the sentence to allow it to be served on consecutive days.
@ref s 732(2) (src:15513-15514)
GIVEN `the offender is ordered to serve a sentence of imprisonment intermittently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender gives notice to the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732(2) the offender may apply to the court that imposed the sentence to allow it to be served on consecutive days` MEANS   -- gate: on (giving notice to the prosecutor)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender is ordered to serve a sentence of imprisonment intermittently` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offender who is ordered to serve a sentence of imprisonment intermittently may"
        IF NOT `the offender gives notice to the prosecutor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, on giving notice to the prosecutor, apply to the court that imposed the sentence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15515 | Court may vary intermittent sentence if subsequent offence
-- src:15516 | (3) Where a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on a person who is subject to an intermittent sentence in respect of another offence, the unexpired portion of the intermittent sentence shall be served on consecutive days unless the court otherwise orders.
@ref s 732(3) (src:15515-15516)
GIVEN `a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on a person who is subject to an intermittent sentence in respect of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732(3) the unexpired portion of the intermittent sentence is to be served on consecutive days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on a person who is subject to an intermittent sentence in respect of another offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment on a person who is subject to an intermittent sentence in respect of another offence"
        IF `the court otherwise orders` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court otherwise orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 732.1 -- Conditions of a probation order (subsections (2) to (7))`

-- (2): the compulsory conditions. "(a.1)", "(2.1)" and "(2.2)" are shown repealed.
-- src:15521 | Compulsory conditions of probation order
-- src:15522 | (2) The court shall prescribe, as conditions of a probation order, that the offender do all of the following:
-- src:15523 | (a) keep the peace and be of good behaviour;
-- src:15524 | (a.1) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 297]
-- src:15525 | (b) appear before the court when required to do so by the court; and
-- src:15526 | (c) notify the court or the probation officer in advance of any change of name or address, and promptly notify the court or the probation officer of any change of employment or occupation.
@ref s 732.1(2) (src:15521-15526)
DECLARE `s 732.1(2) compulsory condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 732.1(2)(a) keep the peace and be of good behaviour`
    `s 732.1(2)(b) appear before the court when required to do so by the court`
    `s 732.1(2)(c) notify the court or the probation officer in advance of any change of name or address, and promptly notify them of any change of employment or occupation`
    `s 732.1(2) another condition`

@ref s 732.1(2) (src:15521-15526)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      condition IS A `s 732.1(2) compulsory condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(2) the court must prescribe the condition as a condition of the probation order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court shall prescribe, as conditions of a probation order"
        IF condition EQUALS `s 732.1(2) another condition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "that the offender do all of the following"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15524 | (a.1) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 297]
@ref s 732.1(2)(a.1) (src:15524)
`s 732.1(2)(a.1), repealed` MEANS "[Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 297]"

-- src:15527 | (2.1) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 297]
@ref s 732.1(2.1) (src:15527)
`s 732.1(2.1), repealed` MEANS "[Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 297]"

-- src:15528 | (2.2) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 297]
@ref s 732.1(2.2) (src:15528)
`s 732.1(2.2), repealed` MEANS "[Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 297]"

-- (3): the optional conditions the court may prescribe. (f) and (h) have limits of their own and are separate functions below.
-- src:15529 | Optional conditions of probation order
-- src:15530 | (3) The court may prescribe, as additional conditions of a probation order, that the offender do one or more of the following:
-- src:15531 | (a) report to a probation officer
-- src:15532 | (i) within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the probation order, and
-- src:15533 | (ii) thereafter, when required by the probation officer and in the manner directed by the probation officer;
-- src:15534 | (a.1) abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order or from going to any place or geographic area specified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the court considers necessary;
-- src:15535 | (b) remain within the jurisdiction of the court unless written permission to go outside that jurisdiction is obtained from the court or the probation officer;
-- src:15536 | (c) abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:15537 | (c.1) provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or someone designated under subsection (9) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to believe that the offender has breached a condition of the order that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:15538 | (c.2) provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified by a probation officer in a notice in Form 51 served on the offender, if a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:15539 | (d) abstain from owning, possessing or carrying a weapon;
-- src:15540 | (e) provide for the support or care of dependants;
-- src:15541 | (f) perform up to 240 hours of community service over a period not exceeding eighteen months;
-- src:15542 | (g) if the offender agrees, and subject to the program director’s acceptance of the offender, participate actively in a treatment program approved by the province;
-- src:15543 | (g.1) where the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the probation order is made has established a program for curative treatment in relation to the consumption of alcohol or drugs, attend at a treatment facility, designated by the lieutenant governor in council of the province, for assessment and curative treatment in relation to the consumption by the offender of alcohol or drugs that is recommended pursuant to the program;
-- src:15544 | (g.2) where the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the probation order is made has established a program governing the use of an alcohol ignition interlock device by an offender and if the offender agrees to participate in the program, comply with the program; and
-- src:15545 | (h) comply with such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable, subject to any regulations made under subsection 738(2), for protecting society and for facilitating the offender’s successful reintegration into the community.
@ref s 732.1(3) (src:15529-15545)
DECLARE `s 732.1(3) optional condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 732.1(3)(a) report to a probation officer within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the probation order, and thereafter when required by the probation officer`
    `s 732.1(3)(a.1) abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order or from going to any place or geographic area specified in the order`
    `s 732.1(3)(b) remain within the jurisdiction of the court unless written permission to go outside it is obtained from the court or the probation officer`
    `s 732.1(3)(c) abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance`
    `s 732.1(3)(c.1) provide a sample of a bodily substance on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or a person designated to make a demand`
    `s 732.1(3)(c.2) provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified by a probation officer in a notice in Form 51`
    `s 732.1(3)(d) abstain from owning, possessing or carrying a weapon`
    `s 732.1(3)(e) provide for the support or care of dependants`
    `s 732.1(3)(f) perform community service`
    `s 732.1(3)(g) participate actively in a treatment program approved by the province`
    `s 732.1(3)(g.1) attend at a treatment facility designated by the lieutenant governor in council for assessment and curative treatment`
    `s 732.1(3)(g.2) comply with a program governing the use of an alcohol ignition interlock device`
    `s 732.1(3)(h) comply with such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable`
    `s 732.1(3) another kind of condition`

@ref s 732.1(3) (src:15529-15545)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      condition IS A `s 732.1(3) optional condition`
      `the offender agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program director accepts the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the probation order is made has established the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(3) the court may prescribe the condition as an additional condition of the probation order` MEANS   -- gate: where (g.1 and g.2: the lieutenant governor in council has established a program); if (c.2, g and g.2)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may prescribe, as additional conditions of a probation order"
        IF condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3) another kind of condition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "one or more of the following"
        IF (condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3)(g.1) attend at a treatment facility designated by the lieutenant governor in council for assessment and curative treatment`) AND (NOT `the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the probation order is made has established the program`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the probation order is made has established a program for curative treatment"
        IF (condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3)(g.2) comply with a program governing the use of an alcohol ignition interlock device`) AND (NOT `the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the probation order is made has established the program`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the probation order is made has established a program governing the use of an alcohol ignition interlock device"
        IF (condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3)(g) participate actively in a treatment program approved by the province`) AND (NOT `the offender agrees`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the offender agrees"
        IF (condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3)(g) participate actively in a treatment program approved by the province`) AND (NOT `the program director accepts the offender`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the program director's acceptance of the offender"
        IF (condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3)(g.2) comply with a program governing the use of an alcohol ignition interlock device`) AND (NOT `the offender agrees`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the offender agrees to participate in the program"
        IF (condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3)(c.2) provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified by a probation officer in a notice in Form 51`) AND (NOT `a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3)(f): "up to 240 hours of community service over a period not exceeding eighteen months": limits the text closes in its own words.
@ref s 732.1(3)(f) (src:15541)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of community service` IS A NUMBER
      `the period in months over which the community service is to be performed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(3)(f) the court may prescribe the community service as an additional condition of the probation order` MEANS   -- gate: limits of the grant (up to 240 hours, a period not exceeding eighteen months)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may prescribe, as additional conditions of a probation order"
        IF (`the hours of community service` GREATER THAN 240) OR (`the period in months over which the community service is to be performed` GREATER THAN 18) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "perform up to 240 hours of community service over a period not exceeding eighteen months"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 732.1(3)(h) (src:15545)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is reasonable and the court considers it desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is for protecting society and for facilitating the offender's successful reintegration into the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation made under subsection 738(2) bars the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(3)(h) the court may prescribe the other condition as an additional condition of the probation order` MEANS   -- gate: subject to (regulations under subsection 738(2))
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may prescribe, as additional conditions of a probation order"
        IF `a regulation made under subsection 738(2) bars the condition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any regulations made under subsection 738(2)"
        IF NOT (`the condition is reasonable and the court considers it desirable` AND `the condition is for protecting society and for facilitating the offender's successful reintegration into the community`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "comply with such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3)(a): the offender's duty to report, where the court has prescribed that condition: "within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs".
-- The duty is also a regulative rule; the number of days is an input (working days are counted by the caller).
-- src:15531 | (a) report to a probation officer
-- src:15532 | (i) within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the probation order, and
-- src:15533 | (ii) thereafter, when required by the probation officer and in the manner directed by the probation officer;
@ref s 732.1(3)(a) (src:15531-15533)
DECLARE `s 732.1(3)(a) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 732.1(3)(a)(i) report to a probation officer after the making of the probation order`

@ref s 732.1(3)(a)(i) (src:15531-15532)
GIVEN `the court prescribed the condition in paragraph 732.1(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days within which the offender must report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 732.1(3)(a) action`
`s 732.1(3)(a)(i) the offender's duty to report to a probation officer after the making of the order` MEANS
    IF `the court prescribed the condition in paragraph 732.1(3)(a)`
    THEN PARTY `the offender` MUST `s 732.1(3)(a)(i) report to a probation officer after the making of the probation order`
         WITHIN `the number of days within which the offender must report`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the offender` BECAUSE "the offender did not report to a probation officer within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the probation order"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 732.1(3)(a)(i) (src:15531-15532)
GIVEN `the court prescribed the condition in paragraph 732.1(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(3)(a)(i) the offender must report to a probation officer after the making of the order` MEANS
    IF `the court prescribed the condition in paragraph 732.1(3)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may prescribe, as additional conditions of a probation order, that the offender do one or more of the following"

-- (3.1): the optional conditions for an organization.
-- src:15546 | Optional conditions — organization
-- src:15547 | (3.1) The court may prescribe, as additional conditions of a probation order made in respect of an organization, that the offender do one or more of the following:
-- src:15548 | (a) make restitution to a person for any loss or damage that they suffered as a result of the offence;
-- src:15549 | (b) establish policies, standards and procedures to reduce the likelihood of the organization committing a subsequent offence;
-- src:15550 | (c) communicate those policies, standards and procedures to its representatives;
-- src:15551 | (d) report to the court on the implementation of those policies, standards and procedures;
-- src:15552 | (e) identify the senior officer who is responsible for compliance with those policies, standards and procedures;
-- src:15553 | (f) provide, in the manner specified by the court, the following information to the public, namely,
-- src:15554 | (i) the offence of which the organization was convicted,
-- src:15555 | (ii) the sentence imposed by the court, and
-- src:15556 | (iii) any measures that the organization is taking — including any policies, standards and procedures established under paragraph (b) — to reduce the likelihood of it committing a subsequent offence; and
-- src:15557 | (g) comply with any other reasonable conditions that the court considers desirable to prevent the organization from committing subsequent offences or to remedy the harm caused by the offence.
@ref s 732.1(3.1) (src:15546-15557)
DECLARE `s 732.1(3.1) optional condition for an organization` IS ONE OF
    `s 732.1(3.1)(a) make restitution to a person for any loss or damage that they suffered as a result of the offence`
    `s 732.1(3.1)(b) establish policies, standards and procedures to reduce the likelihood of the organization committing a subsequent offence`
    `s 732.1(3.1)(c) communicate those policies, standards and procedures to its representatives`
    `s 732.1(3.1)(d) report to the court on the implementation of those policies, standards and procedures`
    `s 732.1(3.1)(e) identify the senior officer who is responsible for compliance with those policies, standards and procedures`
    `s 732.1(3.1)(f) provide to the public, in the manner specified by the court, the offence, the sentence and the measures the organization is taking`
    `s 732.1(3.1)(g) comply with any other reasonable conditions that the court considers desirable to prevent the organization from committing subsequent offences or to remedy the harm caused by the offence`
    `s 732.1(3.1) another kind of condition`

@ref s 732.1(3.1) (src:15546-15557)
GIVEN `the probation order is made in respect of an organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      condition IS A `s 732.1(3.1) optional condition for an organization`
      `the other condition is reasonable and the court considers it desirable to prevent the organization from committing subsequent offences or to remedy the harm caused by the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(3.1) the court may prescribe the condition as an additional condition of the probation order made in respect of an organization` MEANS   -- gate: none (the limit is on the order, an organization)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the probation order is made in respect of an organization` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "additional conditions of a probation order made in respect of an organization"
        IF condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3.1) another kind of condition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "one or more of the following"
        IF (condition EQUALS `s 732.1(3.1)(g) comply with any other reasonable conditions that the court considers desirable to prevent the organization from committing subsequent offences or to remedy the harm caused by the offence`) AND (NOT `the other condition is reasonable and the court considers it desirable to prevent the organization from committing subsequent offences or to remedy the harm caused by the offence`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other reasonable conditions that the court considers desirable to prevent the organization from committing subsequent offences or to remedy the harm caused by the offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15558 | Consideration — organizations
-- src:15559 | (3.2) Before making an order under paragraph (3.1)(b), a court shall consider whether it would be more appropriate for another regulatory body to supervise the development or implementation of the policies, standards and procedures referred to in that paragraph.
@ref s 732.1(3.2) (src:15558-15559)
GIVEN `the court is about to make an order under paragraph 732.1(3.1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(3.2) the court must consider whether another regulatory body would be more appropriate to supervise the policies, standards and procedures` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to make an order under paragraph 732.1(3.1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before making an order under paragraph (3.1)(b), a court shall consider"

-- src:15560 | Form and period of order
-- src:15561 | (4) A probation order may be in Form 46, and the court that makes the probation order shall specify therein the period for which it is to remain in force.
@ref s 732.1(4) (src:15560-15561)
GIVEN `the probation order is in Form 46` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(4) a probation order may be in Form 46` MEANS   -- gate: none
    IF `the probation order is in Form 46`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A probation order may be in Form 46"

@ref s 732.1(4) (src:15560-15561)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(4) the court must specify the period for which the order is to remain in force` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a probation order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court that makes the probation order shall specify therein the period for which it is to remain in force"

-- (5): the court's obligations on making a probation order.
-- src:15562 | Obligations of court
-- src:15563 | (5) The court that makes a probation order shall
-- src:15564 | (a) cause a copy of the order to be given to the offender and, on request, to the victim;
@ref s 732.1(5)(a) (src:15562-15564)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(5)(a) the court must cause a copy of the order to be given to the offender` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a probation order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court that makes a probation order shall (a) cause a copy of the order to be given to the offender"

@ref s 732.1(5)(a) (src:15562-15564)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim requests a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(5)(a) the court must cause a copy of the order to be given to the victim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court makes a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court that makes a probation order shall"
        IF NOT `the victim requests a copy` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and, on request, to the victim"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15565 | (b) explain the conditions of the order set under subsections (2) to (3.1) and the substance of section 733.1 to the offender;
@ref s 732.1(5)(b) (src:15565)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(5)(b) the court must explain the conditions of the order and the substance of section 733.1 to the offender` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a probation order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court that makes a probation order shall"

-- src:15566 | (c) cause an explanation to be given to the offender of the procedure for applying under subsection 732.2(3) for a change to the optional conditions and of the substance of subsections 732.2(3) and (5); and
@ref s 732.1(5)(c) (src:15566)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(5)(c) the court must cause an explanation to be given to the offender of the procedure for applying for a change to the optional conditions` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a probation order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court that makes a probation order shall"

-- src:15567 | (d) take reasonable measures to ensure that the offender understands the order and the explanations.
@ref s 732.1(5)(d) (src:15567)
GIVEN `the court makes a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(5)(d) the court must take reasonable measures to ensure that the offender understands the order and the explanations` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a probation order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court that makes a probation order shall"

-- src:15568 | For greater certainty
-- src:15569 | (6) For greater certainty, a failure to comply with subsection (5) does not affect the validity of the probation order.
@ref s 732.1(6) (src:15568-15569)
GIVEN `the court failed to comply with subsection 732.1(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(6) the failure leaves the validity of the probation order unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the court failed to comply with subsection 732.1(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a failure to comply with subsection (5) does not affect the validity of the probation order"

-- (7): the notice for samples at regular intervals.
-- src:15570 | Notice — samples at regular intervals
-- src:15571 | (7) The notice referred to in paragraph (3)(c.2) must specify the places and times at which and the days on which the offender must provide samples of a bodily substance under a condition described in that paragraph. The first sample may not be taken earlier than 24 hours after the offender is served with the notice, and subsequent samples must be taken at regular intervals of at least seven days.
@ref s 732.1(7) (src:15570-15571)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the places at which the offender must provide samples` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the times at which the offender must provide samples` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the days on which the offender must provide samples` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(7) the notice specifies what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the places at which the offender must provide samples` AND `the notice specifies the times at which the offender must provide samples` AND `the notice specifies the days on which the offender must provide samples`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice referred to in paragraph (3)(c.2) must specify the places and times at which and the days on which the offender must provide samples of a bodily substance"

@ref s 732.1(7) (src:15570-15571)
GIVEN `the hours between service of the notice and the first sample` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(7) the first sample is taken as the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the hours between service of the notice and the first sample` AT LEAST 24
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first sample may not be taken earlier than 24 hours after the offender is served with the notice"

@ref s 732.1(7) (src:15570-15571)
GIVEN `the subsequent samples are taken at regular intervals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days between one sample and the next` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(7) the subsequent samples are taken as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the subsequent samples are taken at regular intervals` AND (`the days between one sample and the next` AT LEAST 7)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsequent samples must be taken at regular intervals of at least seven days"

-- (8), (9) and (12) are regulation-making and designation machinery (inert, reason 2). (10) is a restriction and (11) a duty, and both are encoded.
-- src:15584 | Restriction
-- src:15585 | (10) Samples of bodily substances referred to in paragraphs (3)(c.1) and (c.2) may not be taken, analyzed, stored, handled or destroyed, and the records of the results of the analysis of the samples may not be protected or destroyed, except in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (8).
@ref s 732.1(10) (src:15584-15585)
GIVEN `the act is the taking, analysing, storing, handling or destroying of a sample of a bodily substance referred to in paragraph 732.1(3)(c.1) or (c.2), or the protecting or destroying of the records of the results of the analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is done in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection 732.1(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(10) the act is done in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection 732.1(8)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act is the taking, analysing, storing, handling or destroying of a sample of a bodily substance referred to in paragraph 732.1(3)(c.1) or (c.2), or the protecting or destroying of the records of the results of the analysis` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Samples of bodily substances referred to in paragraphs (3)(c.1) and (c.2) may not be taken, analyzed, stored, handled or destroyed"
        IF `the act is done in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection 732.1(8)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be taken, analyzed, stored, handled or destroyed, and the records of the results of the analysis of the samples may not be protected or destroyed, except in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (8)"

-- (11): the duty to cause samples to be destroyed within the periods prescribed by regulation "unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence".
-- The period is prescribed by regulation outside this text, so the number of days is an input. There is no Party for the minister of justice of a territory in the core;
-- the generic `the Attorney General` stands for both (recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:15586 | Destruction of samples
-- src:15587 | (11) The Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory, or a person authorized by the Attorney General or minister, shall cause all samples of bodily substances provided under a probation order to be destroyed within the periods prescribed by regulation unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 733.1.
@ref s 732.1(11) (src:15586-15587)
DECLARE `s 732.1(11) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 732.1(11) cause all samples of bodily substances provided under a probation order to be destroyed`

@ref s 732.1(11) (src:15586-15587)
GIVEN `samples of bodily substances were provided under a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 733.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of the period prescribed by regulation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 732.1(11) action`
`s 732.1(11) the Attorney General's duty to cause the samples to be destroyed` MEANS
    IF `samples of bodily substances were provided under a probation order` AND (NOT `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 733.1`)
    THEN PARTY `the Attorney General` MUST `s 732.1(11) cause all samples of bodily substances provided under a probation order to be destroyed`
         WITHIN `the number of days of the period prescribed by regulation`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Attorney General` BECAUSE "the samples were not destroyed within the periods prescribed by regulation"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 732.1(11) (src:15586-15587)
GIVEN `samples of bodily substances were provided under a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 733.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732.1(11) the Attorney General must cause the samples to be destroyed within the periods prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `samples of bodily substances were provided under a probation order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall cause all samples of bodily substances provided under a probation order to be destroyed"
        IF `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 733.1` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 733.1"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
